  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Populoside B may exert its biological effects on HepG2 through a series of target-mediated pathways. The drug is predicted to interact with CEM, which in turn targets Loperamide oxide, and this compound further targets HepG2. Similarly, Populoside B is also predicted to interact with ASPC1, which is targeted by a complex compound, and this complex also targets HepG2. Additionally, Populoside B is predicted to interact with Phosphatidylserine synthase 1, which is targeted by Garcinielliptone L, and this compound also targets HepG2. These findings collectively indicate that Populoside B may act as a potential modulator of HepG2 through multiple downstream targets, possibly by influencing signaling pathways or cellular processes that are relevant to the cell line. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism of action involving the modulation of key enzymes or receptors, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated."
